<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sword of Goujian</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">5th century BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sword of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goujian">Goujian</a> is a bronze sword of the State of Yue found in 1965 in a Chu tomb near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiangling">Jiangling</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hubei">Hubei</a>. An inscription in bird-script names its owner as a king of Yue, identified as Goujian, who reigned from 496 to 465 BCE. Still sharp and untarnished, with fine diamond patterning on the blade, it is held in the Hubei Provincial Museum.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sword-of-goujian.jpg" alt="Sword of Goujian" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Windmemories · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:20230208_Bronze_sword_used_by_King_Goujian_of_Yue_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
